Interoperability
QuestBridge talks to Meta Quest headsets over the wired Link protocol so that
they work with computers and software that Meta's own PC app doesn't support.
The protocol was studied from USB traffic between the author's own devices.
QuestBridge contains no code from Meta.

Test data
tests/fixtures/ contains short protocol messages recorded from the author's own
devices. They are kept for byte-exact interoperability tests. Device serial
numbers, device ids, UUIDs and network addresses were replaced with
placeholders, and the recorded video frame carries no picture content.
docs/protocol/schemas/ lists message field names and ids as they appear on the
wire, kept for the same purpose.

